@*
    A badge is `badge` plus the kind it belongs to, and optionally the value it
    holds — `badge badge--status badge--status-ready`. StatusBadge and
    PriorityBadge are this component with the slug already worked out.

    A host with its own badge naming replaces `badge` through `BaseClass`; with
    no kind the modifier collapses to `<base>--<slug>`, which is what a plain
    one-dimensional badge looks like.

    What element it renders depends on what the host can do with the value, not on
    what the value is — the tri-state KnowledgeReferenceLink and IntegrationLink
    already draw, and the third copy of it rather than a fourth shape. Given a URL
    it is an anchor, given a callback it is a button, given neither it is the span
    every badge in this library has always been. The argument is the one recorded
    on those two: an anchor can be middle-clicked, copied and opened in a new
    window and a button cannot, and a value nobody can follow should not invite a
    click or take a tab stop to refuse one.

    A badge earns it because some badges name something a reader wants to go to. An
    alias is the case that forced it: it applies to a term, and a host that knows
    where that term is modelled should be able to say so. A second badge
    implementation with an href on it — which is the alternative — would be a
    parallel tone scale nobody would keep in step with this one.

    The span is written last and unchanged. Every existing caller passes neither
    parameter and so renders exactly the markup it always did, down to the
    attribute order.
*@

@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Href))
{
    <a class="@ClassValue" href="@Href" data-testid="@TestId" title="@Title" @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">@ChildContent</a>
}
else if (OnClick.HasDelegate)
{
    <button type="button" class="@ClassValue" data-testid="@TestId" title="@Title" @onclick="OnClick" @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">@ChildContent</button>
}
else
{
    <span class="@ClassValue" data-testid="@TestId" title="@Title" @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">@ChildContent</span>
}

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public string Kind { get; set; } = "status";

    [Parameter]
    public string? Slug { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? Title { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Where the value leads. Only the host knows whether a badge's value
    /// has an address, so it hands one in rather than this component deriving one
    /// from the text.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Href { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised when the badge is activated. Ignored while
    /// <see cref="Href"/> is set: a link already navigates, and two ways to reach
    /// one place is one too many.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<MouseEventArgs> OnClick { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>badge</c> as the class every badge carries.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string BaseClass { get; set; } = "badge";

    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object>? AdditionalAttributes { get; set; }

    private string ClassValue
    {
        get
        {
            var kind = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Kind) ? string.Empty : $" {BaseClass}--{Kind}";
            var slug = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Slug)
                ? string.Empty
                : string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Kind)
                    ? $" {BaseClass}--{Slug}"
                    : $" {BaseClass}--{Kind}-{Slug}";
            var extra = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? string.Empty : " " + CssClass;

            return $"{BaseClass}{kind}{slug}{extra}";
        }
    }
}
